1
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:13,340
Try letting peace go
lightly and stepping away.

2
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:26,880
Aiming for a certain day
floating on the Nakagawa.

3
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:33,980
Kick a pebble and even your shoes go flying.

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,240
And to the head carpenter
who had been saving up,

5
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:48,460
they laughed that I was still just a kid.

6
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:53,560
Even if I somehow stir
up some energy somewhere,

7
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:58,640
Katsushika, Kameari,
even a yawn changes nothing.

8
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:02,500
The streetscape feels strangely kind.

9
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:10,460
From the pointed hat, from the water jug,

10
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:16,780
a great celestial circle,
and the sunset sinks.

11
00:01:20,940 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow too will end like this, won't it.

12
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,360
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness is lost once again.

13
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:43,960
The infinite, expanding universe

14
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:48,660
where unknown wonders still exist.

15
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:54,140
For the next thirty minutes,

16
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:58,120
your eyes will leave your body

17
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:01,660
and enter this mysterious time.

18
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:07,280
A gift from the cosmos.

19
00:02:14,060 --> 00:02:19,020
Ryo-chan!

20
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:22,180
If Chief finds you making that kind of thing,
you'll be in big trouble.

21
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:24,920
Relax, I'll finish it
before the Chief gets here.

22
00:02:26,220 --> 00:02:29,780
If only you'd put at least half that
enthusiasm into your actual work.

23
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:36,540
Alright, just one more push.

24
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:51,700
You can eat such hard bone crackers.

25
00:02:52,160 --> 00:02:54,700
Ryo-chan's teeth are as tough as diamonds

26
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:00,720
What?

27
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:15,520
What on earth happened?

28
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:18,020
Looks like something
exploded outside the window.

29
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:19,020
Don't tell me, a bomb?

30
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:22,640
There's a hole!

31
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:27,220
Looks like something fell from the sky.

32
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:28,720
A meteorite, maybe?

33
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:31,180
Let's check it out.

34
00:03:31,180 --> 00:03:33,220
Senpai.

35
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:38,240
It's scattered all over, but it does
seem to be a meteorite after all.

36
00:03:38,620 --> 00:03:41,060
Senpai, you'd better not get too close.

37
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:41,840
You think so?

38
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:44,260
Still, that was close.

39
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:47,960
If it had been a little off, it would
have hit us right when it was ejected.

40
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:49,100
True enough.

41
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:52,860
Hey, the gawkers are piling up.

42
00:03:53,660 --> 00:03:54,820
I'll contact the station.

43
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:56,380
I'll handle the cleanup.

44
00:03:56,580 --> 00:03:59,560
Let's clear out before
this turns into a hassle.

45
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:00,200
Here we go.

46
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:06,840
Noooo! My Zero fighter has been shot down!

47
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:09,620
It can't be helped. It was a work of genius.

48
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:12,820
It was almost finished, too.

49
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:13,520
Damn it!

50
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:22,920
What is this thing?
It's as hard as real rock!

51
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:23,720
Ryo-chan.

52
00:04:25,980 --> 00:04:29,120
Stop eating rice crackers
and help us clean up.

53
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:34,120
Oh no, I have to get up early tomorrow
to watch Ohtsuka-san on Mezamashi TV.

54
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:35,760
Sorry, but I'm leaving the rest to you.

55
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:37,220
That's not fair, Ryo-chan!

56
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:41,160
Whoever runs away first wins.

57
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:44,800
Being the first to find it means they'll pester me with questions,
and that's a hassle.

58
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:52,180
A meteorite with a
different molecular structure?

59
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:53,040
Yes, that's right.

60
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:55,580
It's an unknown substance
that doesn't exist on Earth.

61
00:04:55,580 --> 00:04:57,300
So is it dangerous?

62
00:04:58,260 --> 00:04:59,260
Not so far.

63
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:03,160
A specialist professor is
supposed to come this afternoon.

64
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:04,060
I see.

65
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:09,880
I slept well.

66
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:11,900
Somehow I feel great today.

67
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:13,460
I'm walking on air!

68
00:05:19,060 --> 00:05:19,620
What?

69
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:22,380
It's like I'm floating.

70
00:05:22,380 --> 00:05:22,980
Move!

71
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:23,360
Whoa...

72
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:23,960
Aaah!

73
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:25,760
Aaah!

74
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:26,140
Aaah!

75
00:05:26,140 --> 00:05:26,740
Aaah!

76
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:27,240
Aaah!

77
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:27,580
Aaah!

78
00:05:27,580 --> 00:05:28,160
Aaah!

79
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:28,540
Aaah!

80
00:05:28,540 --> 00:05:29,440
Aaah!

81
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:29,940
Aaah!

82
00:05:29,940 --> 00:05:30,000
Aaah!

83
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:30,060
Aah!

84
00:05:30,060 --> 00:05:30,780
Aah!

85
00:05:30,780 --> 00:05:30,820
Aah!

86
00:05:30,820 --> 00:05:30,960
Aah!

87
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:31,080
Aah!

88
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:31,180
Aah!

89
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:31,580
Aah!

90
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:31,600
Aah!

91
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:31,760
Aah!

92
00:05:35,020 --> 00:05:36,700
What's going on?!

93
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,300
I'm floating in the air!

94
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:48,400
I can't feel any weight at all.

95
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:50,060
What is this?

96
00:05:50,060 --> 00:05:50,960
Ryotsu!

97
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:52,320
Chief!

98
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:54,720
What are you doing up there?

99
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:57,240
That's what I should be asking you!

100
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:58,280
Well, you see...

101
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:14,680
Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh!

102
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:15,980
Crash into it!

103
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:23,240
Where did he go?

104
00:06:29,460 --> 00:06:30,760
It finally stopped.

105
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:34,480
You idiot, get away quickly!

106
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:43,720
Three grams!

107
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:47,040
What's going on? I can't believe this!

108
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:49,060
I don't know what's going on either!

109
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:51,940
Honestly, what a troublemaker you are.

110
00:06:52,260 --> 00:06:56,500
Are you so light that your weight is ridiculous,
not just your behavior?

111
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,780
Don't sneeze at me!

112
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:06,380
Sorry, sorry.

113
00:07:06,380 --> 00:07:08,580
Good thing you had weights on.

114
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:10,740
Honestly, am I a balloon?

115
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:16,140
Still, how on earth did this happen?

116
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:18,480
If I knew that, I wouldn't be struggling.

117
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:30,640
What on earth is that?

118
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:32,760
I've got a bad feeling about this.

119
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:42,140
Oolong tea is the world's finest drink,
produced in Fujian Province, China.

120
00:07:42,620 --> 00:07:43,780
Professor Esaki.

121
00:07:43,780 --> 00:07:45,120
So it's you after all.

122
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:47,660
Ni hao, everyone at the police box!

123
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:51,280
What the hell are you doing here?

124
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:55,560
Xièxie, chāshāo, shāomài,
qīngjiāo ròusī, huíguō ròu.

125
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,120
Stop talking gibberish!

126
00:07:57,920 --> 00:08:01,400
Well, I've been teaching at
Peking University since last month.

127
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:04,280
Chinese just keeps slipping

128
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:06,560
You're just reciting a
Chinese restaurant menu!

129
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:09,620
It's no good,
Japanese people in a short time

130
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:19,040
Four thousand years of Chinese
wisdom flows like the Yangzi River,

131
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:21,360
living at an unhurried pace.

132
00:08:22,260 --> 00:08:23,540
Is he a Sinophile or something?

133
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:26,340
But if a Chinese person saw this,
they'd probably be furious.

134
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:28,740
So, Professor,
what exactly brings you here today?

135
00:08:29,900 --> 00:08:33,900
Yes, I received word that a meteorite
fell somewhere nearby last night.

136
00:08:35,620 --> 00:08:37,840
Then what about the specialist
professor who was supposed to come?

137
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:39,960
You're Professor Esaki?

138
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:42,340
Wasn't your specialty
mechanical engineering?

139
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:45,400
Astrophysics is also the professor's specialty,
you know.

140
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:48,000
Is there something special
about that meteorite?

141
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:53,320
Actually, that meteorite is apparently a special one,
made of an unknown substance.

142
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:56,700
So, has anything unusual
happened since then?

143
00:08:57,140 --> 00:08:58,560
Well, if you're talking
about anything unusual,

144
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:03,260
the only thing is that this idiot's
weight has dropped to just three grams.

145
00:09:03,620 --> 00:09:06,440
That's it! It must be the meteorite's doing!

146
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:12,280
Behold, the meteorite in
question is stuck to this wall.

147
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:14,320
So it is.

148
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:15,180
Ew, no way.

149
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:19,780
This meteorite is made of an anti-gravity
material that does not exist on Earth.

150
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:23,240
That's why your body has become so light.

151
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:24,600
Anti-gravity material?

152
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:26,600
What? What's that supposed to mean?

153
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:31,840
In other words, it's a substance that
repels Earth's gravitational pull.

154
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:35,120
But how did it get inside Senpai's body?

155
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:36,200
How would I know?

156
00:09:36,860 --> 00:09:39,880
He probably picked up something
off the ground and ate it again.

157
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:42,640
Even I wouldn't pick up
a meteorite and eat it...

158
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:46,760
Now that you mention it, back then...

159
00:09:48,900 --> 00:09:50,500
What is this thing?

160
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:52,940
It's as hard as a real rock.

161
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:57,960
So the meteorite got mixed
into that Harakotsu cracker?

162
00:09:57,960 --> 00:09:59,760
That must be it.

163
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:03,200
Can't even tell a cracker from a meteorite

164
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:04,500
But that's strange.

165
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:08,360
A meteorite that should have a
force repelling Earth's gravity,

166
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:10,600
how did it end up falling onto Earth?

167
00:10:11,140 --> 00:10:12,160
Now that you mention it...

168
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:16,100
In other words,
a certain kind of amino acid is involved.

169
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:17,380
Amino acid?

170
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:21,520
You! After you took the meteorite into your body last night,
did you eat anything?

171
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:23,860
Stir-fried liver and chives, maybe?

172
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:28,520
That's it! The meteorite and the stir-fried liver fused together in his stomach,
and as a result,

173
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:32,580
the anti-gravity properties manifested.
Beautiful.

174
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:34,640
Is that so?

175
00:10:35,580 --> 00:10:37,540
Somehow, I just can't trust that.

176
00:10:38,340 --> 00:10:39,680
What?

177
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:40,980
W-wait, hey!

178
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:41,960
Ryo-chan!

179
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:44,600
What's going on?

180
00:10:45,060 --> 00:10:48,320
Looks like his anti-gravity
power is growing.

181
00:10:48,320 --> 00:10:52,020
At this rate, he'll break through the atmosphere
and end up in outer space.

182
00:10:52,020 --> 00:10:54,920
This is no joke! Please, do something!

183
00:10:56,100 --> 00:10:57,800
You're really lucky.

184
00:10:58,520 --> 00:11:04,000
Because I happen to hold the secret scroll

185
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,020
that passes down the recipe for a
4,000-year-old Chinese herbal elixir.

186
00:11:07,060 --> 00:11:10,520
Why herbal medicine?
Wasn't it supposed to be space physics?

187
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:13,022
Young man,
don't underestimate Chinese herbal medicine.

188
00:11:13,072 --> 00:11:15,260
Herbal medicine cures everything.

189
00:11:15,340 --> 00:11:16,660
That's not what I meant.

190
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:22,619
I understand. The medicine we give this man,

191
00:11:22,669 --> 00:11:27,180
it's a medicine that cures
any symptom in one dose.

192
00:11:27,380 --> 00:11:31,080
Once he takes this, the effects of the
meteorite will vanish without a trace.

193
00:11:32,380 --> 00:11:34,240
That's not convincing at all.

194
00:11:35,620 --> 00:11:38,420
Fine, then.
I'll just go back to China like this.

195
00:11:38,420 --> 00:11:42,080
Eeeeeeh, wait!
Fine, fine, just give him that stuff!

196
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:47,520
Please, Professor. Since science can't do anything,
we have no choice but to rely on the mysteries of the East.

197
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:49,900
Please, don't abandon Ryo-chan!

198
00:11:49,900 --> 00:11:53,880
Well, if a cute student and a beautiful Kuunyan ask me,
I can't refuse.

199
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:55,200
Then, right away.

200
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:57,660
Before that, it's tea time.

201
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:04,160
This is truly...

202
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:06,500
Well, you're really saying something.

203
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:22,520
Hōju Katō

204
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:23,660
to what's been grated from Hōju Katō,

205
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:26,280
mix in bat droppings and panda fur,

206
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:27,940
and quickly stir-fry over high heat.

207
00:12:27,940 --> 00:12:30,900
Then add Sichuan pepper
powder and viper extract,

208
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:32,620
and once smoke starts rising,

209
00:12:32,620 --> 00:12:33,960
pour in the laojiu.

210
00:12:35,260 --> 00:12:36,580
The Flame Chef.

211
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:38,140
Korosuke Esaki

212
00:12:39,420 --> 00:12:40,500
When did you become a chef?

213
00:12:40,860 --> 00:12:42,180
Hey, quiet down!

214
00:12:42,260 --> 00:12:43,420
Sorry.

215
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:46,400
Then put a drop lid on it and
let it simmer for three minutes.

216
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:47,840
And it's done!

217
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:52,620
What is this smell?

218
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:54,620
It's making my nose twist!

219
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:56,520
Well, drink up.

220
00:12:56,520 --> 00:12:58,640
I have to drink this?

221
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:01,700
Don't worry, it should be
easier to drink than green juice.

222
00:13:01,700 --> 00:13:04,720
Suck it up, Ryo-zu!
This is no time to be picky!

223
00:13:04,940 --> 00:13:07,780
Fine, fine, whatever happens!

224
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,700
I can't take this anymore!

225
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:19,880
Senpai!

226
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:20,620
Ryo-chan!

227
00:13:23,540 --> 00:13:24,900
He's coming down!

228
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:26,560
It worked!

229
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,600
We did it, his feet touched the floor!

230
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:32,980
Ryo-chan, get on the scale!

231
00:13:35,300 --> 00:13:38,240
Chief, we did it!
He's completely back to normal.

232
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:40,480
I'm so glad, Senpai!

233
00:13:41,660 --> 00:13:46,500
Ryotsu, nothing is impossible
for 4,000 years of Chinese history.

234
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:48,240
How about that?

235
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:55,960
Saved! So even the crackpot professor's
inventions can sometimes be sensible.

236
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,160
I've got a new respect for you.

237
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:00,780
Here I go.

238
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:02,160
Let's do it.

239
00:14:03,420 --> 00:14:04,120
Wait!

240
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,620
Oh crap, it's the cops!

241
00:14:07,160 --> 00:14:09,640
Don't think you can run from
me once I've spotted you!

242
00:14:19,940 --> 00:14:23,780
Maybe it's because I was light before.
Somehow my body feels heavy.

243
00:14:27,460 --> 00:14:28,980
What a light-footed guy you are.

244
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:30,880
Thief! Give up!

245
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:38,580
Heh, you're out of luck. Getting caught by the nimble
Kankichi Ryotsu of Katsushika was your misfortune.

246
00:14:40,300 --> 00:14:43,020
What's going on? My body suddenly got heavy!

247
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:44,200
It's hard to breathe!

248
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:51,780
Hey! Wait!

249
00:14:53,140 --> 00:14:54,520
My body won't move!

250
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:59,260
Damn that Professor!
Now I've gone and gotten heavy instead!

251
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:02,820
What on earth do you weigh?

252
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:09,600
If I can get this far...

253
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:14,660
He's chasing me!

254
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:20,500
It's like I'm running
with a barbell on my back.

255
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:22,660
What a monster!

256
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:24,880
Wait!

257
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:27,600
What a weight!

258
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:30,060
At this rate,
the culprit's going to get away.

259
00:15:38,700 --> 00:15:40,000
It's a downhill slope!

260
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,720
If it comes to this,
rolling down would be faster.

261
00:15:46,660 --> 00:15:48,660
Not yet! But stop!

262
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:05,720
It's so heavy, I can't get up!

263
00:16:05,720 --> 00:16:06,840
Help me!

264
00:16:09,860 --> 00:16:11,540
What? 800 kilos!?

265
00:16:12,160 --> 00:16:12,720
No way!

266
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:14,580
That's ridiculous!

267
00:16:14,660 --> 00:16:15,940
Senpai, are you all right?

268
00:16:16,660 --> 00:16:17,420
Of course I'm not all right!

269
00:16:17,740 --> 00:16:21,440
It's over one ton!

270
00:16:24,180 --> 00:16:26,540
A scale that doesn't break even
when an elephant stands on it!

271
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:31,380
Circling! Circling!

272
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:32,640
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

273
00:16:33,280 --> 00:16:36,160
Where on earth do you
keep finding these extras?!

274
00:16:37,820 --> 00:16:38,805
No, Aoi.

275
00:16:38,855 --> 00:16:44,180
The Chinese Mukan Desert also means once you enter,
you can never leave!

276
00:16:44,180 --> 00:16:47,200
Hey! Because you made me drink
that weird herbal medicine,

277
00:16:47,250 --> 00:16:49,860
now my body keeps getting heavier!

278
00:16:50,940 --> 00:16:53,820
W-we're getting heavy again...

279
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:58,780
Hahaha! I predicted this would happen!
No need to worry!

280
00:16:58,820 --> 00:17:00,260
You knew this would happen!
Do something about it!

281
00:17:00,580 --> 00:17:03,580
Rest assured.
Once you drink this, you'll be fine.

282
00:17:04,380 --> 00:17:08,620
The phantom elixir Chinese
immortals used to fly through the sky!

283
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,340
Just drink it quickly, whatever it is! Hey!

284
00:17:11,340 --> 00:17:11,980
Aaaaaah!

285
00:17:13,140 --> 00:17:21,100
Oops, I mixed up the other medicine with the candy meant for tea...
Which one is it? No need to worry!

286
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:29,020
Hurry up and drink it! This one?
Are you sure? It's definitely right!

287
00:17:29,020 --> 00:17:30,480
...I can't tell which one it is.

288
00:17:32,280 --> 00:17:33,120
Ryotsu

289
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:33,860
Senpai

290
00:17:33,860 --> 00:17:34,980
Ryo-chan

291
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:36,980
My body feels

292
00:17:36,980 --> 00:17:39,020
strangely heavy...

293
00:17:39,020 --> 00:17:40,840
Help me!

294
00:17:41,640 --> 00:17:42,640
Ryotsu

295
00:17:42,640 --> 00:17:43,680
Senpai

296
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:44,960
Ryo-chan

297
00:17:46,420 --> 00:17:47,020
This is

298
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:48,780
What's going on?

299
00:17:49,540 --> 00:17:53,560
There's an abnormal gravitational field being detected,
though it's slight.

300
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:54,580
What?

301
00:18:02,840 --> 00:18:04,000
He's finally stopped.

302
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,600
Sorry, sorry.

303
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:09,140
Looks like I gave him the wrong medicine.

304
00:18:09,140 --> 00:18:11,720
Apparently it reacted with the
meteorite and made him even heavier.

305
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:14,200
What do you mean, it's a medicine
for hermits to fly through the sky?

306
00:18:16,160 --> 00:18:18,160
Even a hermit falls from a tree,
as they say.

307
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:20,180
It's a joke from 4,000
years of Chinese history.

308
00:18:20,180 --> 00:18:21,860
It's monkeys that fall from trees, isn't it?

309
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:24,340
Something's warm down by my feet.

310
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:28,960
Gorilla-kun, it's a hot spring!

311
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:31,880
Look, it's a hot spring! It's a hot spring!

312
00:18:32,420 --> 00:18:34,880
Shime-chan, with this we'll make a fortune!

313
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:38,080
First, we'll build a huge
hot spring resort in Kameari.

314
00:18:38,080 --> 00:18:44,060
Then we'll use the fault line to expand into a
jungle paradise and a tropical botanical garden.

315
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:46,720
Ahahahaha!

316
00:18:48,120 --> 00:18:50,000
But at this rate, I'll drown!

317
00:18:50,620 --> 00:18:52,540
Quick, the medicine!

318
00:18:52,700 --> 00:18:54,702
Right

319
00:18:54,752 --> 00:18:57,120
Um, yeah, this one!

320
00:18:57,120 --> 00:19:00,120
Where is it? Mister Gorilla!

321
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:01,160
Wherever it is.

322
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:04,040
Even if you go to a place like that now,

323
00:19:04,040 --> 00:19:05,740
Fine, just hurry with the medicine!

324
00:19:09,980 --> 00:19:11,300
He's getting heavy again!

325
00:19:13,660 --> 00:19:15,080
We're gonna get grilled for this.

326
00:19:18,620 --> 00:19:20,500
What on earth is causing this?

327
00:19:20,500 --> 00:19:21,560
I don't know.

328
00:19:21,560 --> 00:19:26,620
But it's a fact that some massive
mass is forming on the Eurasian Plate.

329
00:19:27,120 --> 00:19:29,820
This is bad!
Gravity is increasing even more!

330
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:36,120
Exactly! He's gotten even heavier!
What are you going to do about it?!

331
00:19:36,700 --> 00:19:38,180
Do you know something?

332
00:19:38,520 --> 00:19:42,880
The Yangtze river dolphin is a freshwater
dolphin on the brink of extinction!

333
00:19:42,980 --> 00:19:43,820
Don't try to change the subject!

334
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:46,160
What's this?

335
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:49,180
Dinosaur fossils!

336
00:19:49,300 --> 00:19:52,980
And it's a Tyrannosaurus rex that
hasn't been discovered in Japan yet!

337
00:19:53,380 --> 00:19:53,980
Really?

338
00:19:53,980 --> 00:19:57,200
I'm a dinosaur expert,
so there's no mistake about it.

339
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:59,160
Since when did you become a dinosaur expert?

340
00:19:59,980 --> 00:20:01,440
Dinosaur-nan-chatte.

341
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:03,600
Knock it off, you fraud old man!

342
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:06,700
There are more!

343
00:20:06,700 --> 00:20:08,640
This one's a Brachiosaurus.

344
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:10,500
This one's an Euoplocephalus.

345
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:12,160
And this one's a Torinacronmerum.

346
00:20:12,160 --> 00:20:15,760
This is a huge discovery! We can sell
it to dinosaur maniacs for a high price!

347
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:19,540
No, first we build a huge
dinosaur museum in Kamiari.

348
00:20:19,540 --> 00:20:23,700
Then if we expand the business with
character merchandise and a theme park...

349
00:20:27,600 --> 00:20:29,640
This is a newly discovered species,
you know.

350
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:32,220
Let's name it Esaki Kameari Saori.

351
00:20:32,220 --> 00:20:34,000
Put my name in it too!

352
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,940
Well, to celebrate our mutual success,

353
00:20:37,940 --> 00:20:39,960
let's make a toast with tea, shall we?

354
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:42,840
And the candy to go with the tea -

355
00:20:45,400 --> 00:20:47,200
so this was the medicine that made him fly!

356
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:50,300
Hey! Don't leave me behind!

357
00:20:50,300 --> 00:20:52,320
Your change!

358
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,340
Whoa! It's gotten heavy again!

359
00:20:57,460 --> 00:21:00,600
Got it!
Kameari, Japan, 10,000 meters underground!

360
00:21:00,940 --> 00:21:02,360
Kameari!

361
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:04,380
Bringing up the main screen!

362
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:07,775
The object X in question
keeps increasing its mass,

363
00:21:07,825 --> 00:21:09,300
and it's still sinking deeper underground!

364
00:21:09,700 --> 00:21:12,300
If it keeps going like this,
it'll punch through to the mantle layer!

365
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:13,400
Whoa!

366
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:17,100
It's getting hot in here somehow!

367
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:20,000
Whoa! The mantle!

368
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:21,080
Aaagh!

369
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:25,020
Object X has slammed into the mantle layer!
It's being pushed back by the magma!

370
00:21:25,220 --> 00:21:26,900
Mass still increasing!

371
00:21:27,600 --> 00:21:29,180
Damn it! At this rate!

372
00:21:29,360 --> 00:21:30,700
What's going to happen if this continues?!

373
00:21:31,320 --> 00:21:34,498
If object X's mass keeps growing like this,

374
00:21:34,548 --> 00:21:36,880
the Earth's axis is going to tilt!

375
00:21:40,140 --> 00:21:42,400
The Earth's axis has tilted!

376
00:21:42,980 --> 00:21:44,440
Yaaah!

377
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:49,940
It's Hawaii after all, right?

378
00:21:49,940 --> 00:21:51,940
Yeah, that's right.

379
00:21:51,940 --> 00:21:53,300
What's that?

380
00:21:53,660 --> 00:21:54,020
Snow?

381
00:21:58,060 --> 00:22:02,640
This is terrible! Because of the tilt of the axis,
the environment of the entire Earth is changing drastically!

382
00:22:02,780 --> 00:22:04,980
Earthquakes are starting
to happen everywhere!

383
00:22:05,140 --> 00:22:07,000
At this rate, the Earth will... the Earth!

384
00:22:08,220 --> 00:22:08,960
Ryotsu!

385
00:22:09,240 --> 00:22:09,920
Senpai!

386
00:22:10,620 --> 00:22:11,300
Ryo-chan!

387
00:22:25,540 --> 00:22:29,140
As long as object X exists, the Earth
cannot escape the danger of destruction.

388
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:30,320
Please make your decision.

389
00:22:30,320 --> 00:22:31,400
Mr. President.

390
00:22:32,400 --> 00:22:33,040
Understood.

391
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:36,360
Immediately carry out Project Kameari.

392
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:46,120
Here, take it!
The pocket has just been launched!

393
00:22:46,320 --> 00:22:50,900
Wood versus X, who plunged the Earth into peril,
is vanishing into space!

394
00:22:51,400 --> 00:22:53,920
Everyone in the world,
the Earth has been saved!

395
00:22:59,100 --> 00:22:59,740
Chief!

396
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:04,220
How long am I supposed to keep
living in a place like this?

397
00:23:05,180 --> 00:23:08,100
Until the meteorite turns into
poop and comes out of your body.

398
00:23:08,500 --> 00:23:11,880
Or if you'd like,
you might as well stay up there forever.

399
00:23:12,580 --> 00:23:15,280
I want to build model kits like that,
and RC cars too.

400
00:23:15,280 --> 00:23:17,420
I wonder what's going to happen
with next week's horse races.

401
00:23:17,840 --> 00:23:18,980
Don't worry.

402
00:23:18,980 --> 00:23:22,220
In zero gravity,
no matter how heavy you get, you'll be fine.

403
00:23:22,700 --> 00:23:24,280
You can stay here as long as you like.

404
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:26,960
Hey, Professor Crackpot,
what are you doing way out here?

405
00:23:28,440 --> 00:23:31,940
Thanks to that medicine,
I got to space a step ahead of you.

406
00:23:31,940 --> 00:23:35,840
That's right, it's all your fault
for that weird herbal medicine!

407
00:23:35,840 --> 00:23:38,120
It's almost tea time.

408
00:23:39,520 --> 00:23:41,680
Don't be drinking tea all the way out here!

409
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:44,580
Oolong tea tastes especially
good when you drink it in space.

410
00:23:46,140 --> 00:23:49,460
There are still many mysteries in space.

411
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:54,600
You should be careful too when
you eat fossil rice crackers.

412
00:23:54,600 --> 00:24:00,280
Gifts from space may be hidden among them.

413
00:24:05,840 --> 00:24:09,300
Komachi went to the countryside with Nakagawa,
just the two of them?!

414
00:24:09,300 --> 00:24:11,360
Showing off in front of
those disrespectful bunch!

415
00:24:11,720 --> 00:24:17,040
But here's the photo,
undeniable proof, with me in it too!

416
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:19,980
Next time: the dream two-shot!

417
00:24:19,980 --> 00:24:21,440
What will you do, Komachi?

418
00:24:35,840 --> 00:24:44,180
Surprise and commotion, with spirit and resolve,
solved quickly and cut clean.

419
00:24:44,580 --> 00:24:55,680
It's decided, with inspiration, bouncing along,
wrapping up, acting, and flying off.

420
00:24:56,600 --> 00:25:00,380
Above all, an amazing power.

421
00:25:00,380 --> 00:25:12,720
Everyone, gather!
Come here, the dreamlike final energy!

422
00:25:13,720 --> 00:25:23,700
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday, drawing the universe,
standing on the ground, the Kameari star comes spinning round, what a strange thing!

423
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:27,460
This should be good enough, right?

424
00:25:27,460 --> 00:25:28,920
No way it's good enough!

425
00:25:37,580 --> 00:25:40,540
Thank you for watching.

